  "hypothesis": "Hidden intrabasin faults link as relay ramps under present-day extensional strain; a supervised 19-band HistGradientBoosting model trained on visible USGS/INGENIOUS faults vs far-field background learns that geophysical pattern and predicts analogous covered faults as geothermal permeability corridors.",
  "mechanism": "Train HistGradientBoosting (max_iter=150, lr=0.08, max_depth=5) on 19 pinned GeoDAWN bands: rtp, iso_grav_anom, tmi_hg/vg, geodetic second invariant/shear/dilatation, tilt curvature, earthquake distance/intensity, detrended elevation/slope, depth-to-basement, conductivity, gravity gradients. Positives = 60,988 mapped fault pixels; negatives = 80,000 footprint cells >3 px from any mapped fault (unlabelled background). Predict probability over full 3730×3292 grid, mask outside-footprint and on-catalogue to 0, then greedy Poisson place 37,654 dots at 3 px (300 m) spacing by descending probability. No catalogue-distance or borrowed-prediction features enter training; distance filtering only defines background sampling.",
